hyperactivity-is-the-theory-of-knowledge-graphs-lines-68 = cons "**Middle-out DAG and higher-order λ-factoring.** Sequential left-to-right compressors (LZ77, autoregressive scanners) impose an artificial 1D causal arrow and reference only earlier contiguous literal spans. Middle-out compression operates on the relational graph of the whole object from its highest-leverage internal invariants outward in all directions: bidirectional contexts in 1D, full neighborhoods in higher dimensions, and cross-document relations across a corpus. Factoring maximal repeats into content-addressed DAG nodes (`lib/repeats-fast.cub`, `lib/repeats-kasai.cub`, Part I §4.5 `duplicate`, §10.8) shortens the representation at each pass and brings distant correlations into local 1-step adjacency. Because the native objects of hyperactivity are typed interaction nets and λ-terms rather than 0th-order context-free grammars, spans differing at internal holes (A · u · B and A · v · B) factor into a single higher-order abstraction λ x. A · x · B stored once and applied to the differing arguments, capturing parameterized and non-contiguous structure inaccessible to literal dictionary coders." (cons "" nil)
